Yes, you can absolutely give your forked version of Mediasoup a proprietary new brand name.

Mediasoup is distributed under the **ISC License**, which is a highly permissive open-source license (very similar to MIT and BSD). It allows you to freely copy, modify, distribute, and rebrand the software for commercial use.

There is only one legal requirement: you must leave the original copyright notice and the short ISC license text intact in the underlying source code files to acknowledge the original creators (versatica). As long as that text remains in your repository's license file and code headers, you are completely free to rename the project, publish it under your own brand, and use it exclusively for the Live Academy™.

